{"page":"BIRC5","gene":"BIRC5","accession":"O15392","protein":"Baculoviral IAP repeat-containing protein 5","length":142,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"O15392-1","name":"1","synonyms":["Alpha"],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-O15392-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-O15392-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":94.8,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,3],[70,1],[90,84],[70,5],[90,46],[70,2]]}},"features":[{"type":"Repeat","start":18,"end":88,"description":"BIR"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":20,"end":20,"description":"Phosphoserine; by AURKC"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":23,"end":23,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":34,"end":34,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by CDK1 and CDK15"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":48,"end":48,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by CK2; in vitro"},{"type":"Binding site","start":57,"end":57,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":60,"end":60,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":77,"end":77,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":84,"end":84,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":90,"end":90,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":110,"end":110,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":112,"end":112,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":115,"end":115,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":117,"end":117,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by AURKB"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":121,"end":121,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Site","start":126,"end":126,"description":"Interaction with FBXL7"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":129,"end":129,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Monomer or homodimer. Exists as a homodimer in the apo state and as a monomer in the CPC-bound state. The monomer protects cells against apoptosis more efficiently than the dimer. Only the dimeric form is capable of enhancing tubulin stability in cells. When phosphorylated, interacts with LAMTOR5/HBXIP; the resulting complex binds pro-CASP9, as well as active CASP9, but much less efficiently. Component of the chromosomal passenger complex (CPC) composed of at least BIRC5/survivin, CDCA8/borealin, INCENP, AURKB or AURKC; in the complex forms a triple-helix bundle-based subcomplex with INCENP and CDCA8 (PubMed:17956729). Interacts with JTB. Interacts (via BIR domain) with histone H3 phosphorylated at 'Thr-3' (H3pT3). Interacts with EVI5. Interacts with GTP-bound RAN in both the S and M phases of the cell cycle. Interacts with USP9X. Interacts with tubulin. Interacts with BIRC2/c-IAP1. The acetylated form at Lys-129 interacts with STAT3. The monomeric form deacetylated at Lys-129 interacts with XPO1/CRM1. The monomeric form interacts with XIAP/BIRC4. Both the dimeric and monomeric form can interact with DIABLO/SMAC. Interacts with BIRC6/bruce. Interacts with FBXL7; this interaction facilitates the polyubiquitination and subsequent proteasomal degradation of BIRC5 by the SCF(FBXL7) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex (PubMed:25778398, PubMed:28218735)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) EBNA1; this interaction is probably important for EBV episome maintenance in Burkitt's lymphoma cells"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"O15392-2","name":"2","synonyms":["2B","Beta"],"notes":[],"length":165,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,74],[98,75,68]],"edits":[{"start":74,"end":74,"original":"I","replacement":"IGPGTVAYACNTSTLGGRGGRITR","added":24}],"missing":0,"replaced":0,"novel":23,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-O15392-2-F1","cif":"https://alpha